  "question_stem": "{{figure:diagram_q05_01}}\nThe diagram shows a cord going around a pulley and a pin. The pulley is modelled as a circle with centre $O$ and radius 5 cm. The thickness of the cord and the size of the pin $P$ can be neglected. The pin is situated 13 cm vertically below $O$. Points $A$ and $B$ are on the circumference of the circle such that $AP$ and $BP$ are tangents to the circle. The cord passes over the major arc $AB$ of the circle and under the pin such that the cord is taut.",
